<Base
  title="Insurance Denied Your Defense or Coverage?"
  description="Representation for Florida insureds when a liability insurer denies a defense, reserves rights, or mishandles settlement."
>
  <h1>When Your Insurer Denies You</h1>
  <p>
    Liability insurance is a promise of two things: a defense when you
    are sued, and payment of covered claims against you. Disputes arise
    when an insurer refuses to defend, defends under a reservation of
    rights, denies indemnity, or lets a claim that could have settled
    within policy limits turn into a judgment above them.
  </p>
  <p>
    {firm.entity} represents Florida insureds — individuals, property
    owners, contractors, and businesses — in these disputes. Detailed
    pages on denied defenses, reservations of rights, declaratory
    judgment actions, coverage denials, and Florida bad-faith law are in
    preparation; the firm's initial published focus is the
    <a href={href("/personal-injury/")}>personal-injury practice</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    If an insurer has denied or limited your protection now, use the
    <a href={href("/contact/")}>contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
